WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.420
[This tape was duplicated from a 16mm original
by Colorlab for the National Library of Medicine, August 2004, NLM call number HF 783]

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:17.900
[Numbers flash by, counting down.]

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:27.940
[National Motion Pictures Co. presents Your
Health Department, Copyright MCMXLI]

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.500
[Narrator reading from a bas relief:] "The
health of the people is really the foundation

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:37.440
upon which all their happiness and all their
powers as a state depend."

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.800
[Building with "Board of Health" engraved above entrance.]

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:43.720
[Narrator:] Did you ever stop to realize how
much all these health activities mean in your life?

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:52.740
Let's take a look at the Browns. A typical
family whose life and whose problems are not

00:00:52.800 --> 00:01:00.160
so very different from your own.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:05.039
From the very beginning of Frank and Helen
Brown's wedded life, their health department

00:01:05.039 --> 00:01:09.419
has been helping them achieve the blessings
of health and making theirs 

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.780
a more healthful community.

00:01:11.789 --> 00:01:15.590
Before they could obtain a marriage license
in the state where they lived, they had to

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:20.929
show that they were free from venereal infection,
an important factor in their future happiness

00:01:20.929 --> 00:01:24.410
and in the health of any children who might
be born unto them.

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:29.780
The doctor draws a sample of blood for a test.
This should be made a routine part of every

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:35.759
physical examination and must bring to light
many unsuspected cases of syphilis.

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:39.890
In the health department laboratory, the blood
samples submitted by the doctor are tested.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:46.890
At the completion of this test, Frank Brown's sample will show up negative, no syphilis,

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:53.259
but the man who followed him into the doctor's
office has a positive test. This means he

00:01:53.259 --> 00:01:59.509
has syphilis and requires prompt treatment.

00:01:59.509 --> 00:02:05.129
Early continuous treatment will cure syphilis
and prevent its further spread.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:14.800
[A person receives an injection in the arm.]

00:02:16.459 --> 00:02:21.129
Why does the health department come in on
this? It wants to find the contacts of the

00:02:21.129 --> 00:02:26.290
infected man and see that they undergo treatment
if it is necessary.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:31.319
Since continuity of treatment is so essential
for cure, the health authorities are also

00:02:31.319 --> 00:02:37.010
vitally interested in seeing that those under
treatment keep it up until a cure is effected.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:42.370
When their first baby was expected, Mrs. Brown
underwent a blood test as part of her prenatal

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:48.629
examination. Why? Because treatment of expectant
mothers who have syphilis will prevent their

00:02:48.629 --> 00:02:54.780
babies being born with this disease.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.090
Together with other expectant mothers, Mrs.
Brown had the benefit of valuable instruction

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:03.810
given by a competent health nurse.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:09.720
[A nurse stands before a class of students, writing on a chalkboard and pointing to charts on the wall.]

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:15.549
At home, too, Mrs. Brown found the public
health nurse most helpful. This work was carried

00:03:15.549 --> 00:03:22.549
on in complete cooperation with their private
physician.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:28.999
Their first baby was born at home, and the
physician called to engage a maternity nurse

00:03:28.999 --> 00:03:33.829
to assist at delivery, a service offered by
many health departments.

00:03:33.829 --> 00:03:39.599
The nurse helps to prepare for any emergency.
Warming beds or baby incubators must be available

00:03:39.599 --> 00:03:42.999
in case the newborn babe is premature.

00:03:42.999 --> 00:03:47.659
Ready at a moment's notice, the maternity
nurse answers the call, happy in the knowledge

00:03:47.659 --> 00:03:52.170
that she has guided the expectant mother in
healthful living and has helped her prepare

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:56.670
for a safe delivery and a happy convalescence.

00:03:56.780 --> 00:04:04.860
[A nurse carrying her bag of medical supplies emerges from a car and walks up the steps of the house.]

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:13.650
Doing fine, thanks. Each year thousands of
mothers and babies benefit by this maternity

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:20.650
service. Does health work pay? What do you think?

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:28.600
Getting the facts needed for baby's birth
registration.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:35.280
These people are going to a lot of trouble
to obtain birth certificates, which they must

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:40.080
have for employment or for many other reasons.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:50.320
The proper registration of births is of importance to prevent future difficulties.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:55.780
Along with other records, these birth records comprise the vital statistics which serve

00:04:55.790 --> 00:05:01.090
as a guide to health workers, showing them
where they need to put the most effort and

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:04.670
how successful their work has been.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:29.400
[Bar graph with title "Tuberculosis, Deaths
in Five Indiana Counties." 

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:37.300
The health department's work was not completed when the baby was born.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:43.600
It carries through after the birth of the baby. Our suspicion is aroused by a persistent hacking cough.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:49.120
The nurse makes some inquires which lead her
to believe an examination for tuberculosis

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.660
is in order.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:57.480
[Medical form stating "grandmother died of tuberculosis" is shown.]

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:01.260
[A nurse is shown interviewing a woman, then the woman is in a physician's office being guided to an x-ray machine.]

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:09.690
The doctor's thorough examination, which includes
the x-ray, reveals an active case of tuberculosis.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:23.860
Thus, possible infection of the Browns' baby
was prevented and the woman received the treatment

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:29.120
she needed, all because of the thoroughness
of observing and following through, which

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:33.310
are a part of health department training and
practice.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:40.310
All the home contacts of the tubercular woman
are checked carefully.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:47.750
When the baby is six months old, the nurse
reminds Mrs. Brown of the necessity of smallpox

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:54.750
vaccination, and immunization against diphtheria.

00:06:55.960 --> 00:07:00.670
Surely this safe process is more sensible
than running the risk of catching these dangerous

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:06.520
diseases. The Browns' next door neighbors
were guilty of a terrible act of carelessness.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:13.410
They failed to immunize their child against
diphtheria. One day it struck.

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:19.630
[A doctor tends to a child lying in bed at home.]

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:27.300
As soon as the doctor makes a diagnosis of
diphtheria, he gives antitoxin.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:34.080
Sometimes it is necessary to take cultures
on other members of the family to control

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:41.080
the spread of the disease.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:55.540
When a case of communicable disease is reported,
the health department comes into play once more.

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:02.720
It offers laboratory service to confirm
the doctor's diagnosis. It safeguards the

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:05.810
community by isolating the sick individual.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:08.650
[A diptheria quarantine sign is tacked to the front door of a home.]

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:16.020
Once again the public health nurse is of invaluable
help. Here she is instructing the child's

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:23.110
mother on the proper technique to use in the
sickroom. This is important in controlling

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:28.120
the spread of the disease.

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:47.860
[The nurse demonstrates proper handwashing and other care and sanitary practices to the mother.]

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:59.560
The school, of course, is an important place
to work for prevention of spread in many communicable diseases.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:04.800
[A school health staffer is shown checking a girl's throat for signs of illness.]

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:08.740
This work is aided by the use of sanitary
drinking fountains such as these and by rigid

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:12.760
inspection of the entire sanitary system.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:16.480
The school has more than a preventive role to play.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:23.560
It is also an ideal place for teaching the
positive lessons of health. 

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:30.160
Not only by classroom instruction, but by every tried means at its command does the health education department

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:35.870
endeavor to guide the people in the paths
of healthful living.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:40.389
It is not sufficient for science to learn
new facts about nutrition. These facts must

00:09:40.389 --> 00:09:47.310
be brought home to us so that we will learn
how to make use of them in our daily lives.

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:53.699
Since many health faults need correction before
a child is of school age, pre-school examinations,

00:09:53.699 --> 00:09:57.100
dental as well as medical, are of great importance.

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:02.900
The school is a good place to develop a physical
education program, 

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:06.320
which will build strong bodies for our children.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:10.120
[End of Part One]

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:16.220
[Clicking, sputtering sounds.]

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:26.500
[Part Two]

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:37.200
[Numbers flash by, counting down.]

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:43.269
But to return to our friends, the Browns,
the milk they drink, so essential in a healthful

00:10:43.269 --> 00:10:49.120
diet, must be safe milk, carefully guarded
from contamination in every step of its handling

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.949
from the producer to the consumer.

00:10:51.949 --> 00:10:57.290
Healthy cows tested to show they are free
from tuberculosis, mastitis, and contagious

00:10:57.290 --> 00:11:03.170
abortion. Scrupulous cleanliness of the dairy
barn, the cows and the milker's hands. Rinsing

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:07.470
of udders with bactericidal solution.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:18.860
[Man is shown with buckets of liquid, cleaning the cow's udders.

00:11:22.939 --> 00:11:29.939
The inspector makes a thorough check of the
milk house also. Adequate hand-washing facilities.

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:43.620
A stove to heat water for washing and sterilizing
cans and buckets. Check.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:50.009
Clean milk aprons. Check.

00:11:50.009 --> 00:11:57.009
Cabinet for storing strainer pads, chemical
disinfectant, and other loose equipment.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:05.640
Water for cooling milk down to a safe temperature.
Clean buckets and cans. Check.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:11.529
Milk produced under these conditions is clean
milk, but as a further safeguard, it must

00:12:11.529 --> 00:12:13.399
be pasteurized.

00:12:13.399 --> 00:12:17.920
When the milk reaches the pasteurization plant,
it is dumped in properly covered receiving

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:24.920
vats and sampled for tests checking the effectiveness
of the sanitary methods employed in production.

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:42.119
From the receiving tank the milk is transferred
through sanitary piping to the pasteurizer,

00:12:42.119 --> 00:12:47.699
which is equipped with leak-proof inlet and
outlet valves. Each pasteurizer has indicating,

00:12:47.699 --> 00:12:51.379
recording, and air space thermometers.

00:12:51.379 --> 00:12:57.220
After each day's operation, all equipment which
comes in contact with the milk must be disassembled,

00:12:57.220 --> 00:13:00.869
washed and placed upon racks where it remains
for inspection.

00:13:00.869 --> 00:13:06.439
Immediately after being used it is assembled
and sterilized. Dump tanks, filters, pasteurizers,

00:13:06.439 --> 00:13:13.439
sanitary pipes, coolers, bottlers, and individual
bottles must be kept scrupulously clean.

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:20.940
Samples of the producer's milk is analyzed
microscopically by using the breed microscopic technique.]

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:33.180
[A man works with containers and pipettes at a laboratory bench, testing samples.]

00:13:33.649 --> 00:13:39.769
The effectiveness of cooling, the cleanliness
of utensils, and the presence of mastitis

00:13:39.769 --> 00:13:43.849
can be determined by this test.

00:13:43.849 --> 00:13:55.389
[A man peers through a microscope, analyzing a sample.]

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:04.459
After being pasteurized a bacterial plate
count is made of the finished product.

00:14:04.459 --> 00:14:11.459
At this time a phosphotase test is made to determine
the efficiency of pasteurization.

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:27.679
The results of the foregoing precaution in
producing, handling, and processing milk is

00:14:27.679 --> 00:14:34.679
grade A pasteurized milk. When the Browns
eat in a restaurant, their health is safeguarded

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:42.160
by sanitary inspection. Here is a sanitary
inspector checking on dishwashing equipment.

00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:55.429
Pure water is always an important health problem,
but the Browns don't have to worry about that

00:14:55.429 --> 00:15:00.009
because their water comes from the municipal
plant which is subject to constant inspection...

00:15:00.009 --> 00:15:08.860
[An inspector examines equipment at a water treatment facility.]

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:15.860
But, the people who live out in the country
must obtain their water from their own wells.

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:21.420
Properly constructed and located, they are
safe, but many a case of typhoid has been

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:28.420
traced back to a polluted well caused by a cracked platform, split base, and no stuffing box.

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:36.600
The spout is flamed to destroy bacteria and
a sample is collected in a sterilized bottle

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:41.400
which may be obtained from an approved laboratory.

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:44.880
Tested in the health department's water laboratory...

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:54.480
[A man in a lab coat tests small bottles containing water samples, drawing up water into a pipette and distributing droplets into a tray.]

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:59.500
...the water proves to be highly polluted
with colon bacteria, an indication of possible

00:15:59.509 --> 00:16:02.489
typhoid contamination.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:07.140
[A sign reading "Danger, Unfit to Drink" is placed in front of a water pump.]

00:16:07.220 --> 00:16:12.759
Advice on well construction and location is
available to you for the asking. Simply write

00:16:12.759 --> 00:16:18.550
your health department. Another function of
the health department is the inspection of

00:16:18.550 --> 00:16:23.630
swimming pools.

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:30.199
The Browns have a further advantage over their
rural neighbors in the disposal of human waste.

00:16:30.199 --> 00:16:35.079
That problem is taken care of for them by
a municipal sewage disposal plant, which renders

00:16:35.079 --> 00:16:40.179
these wastes non- injurious to health.

00:16:45.220 --> 00:16:50.740
Where water under pressure is not available;
it is impractical to build a septic tank.

00:16:50.749 --> 00:16:57.749
The best solution is a sanitary toilet built
according to health department specification.

00:16:59.429 --> 00:17:04.270
In order to combat those diseases which are
waterborne, the sanitary engineer also works

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:08.770
toward the prevention of stream pollution.
In still another way is his Health Department

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:10.770
interested in Frank Brown's health.

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:15.560
Aroused by a case of silicosis, which occurred
in a fellow worker of his...

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:23.620
...the director of industrial hygiene sends
his inspector to the plant where Frank works

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:26.020
to collect dust samples.

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:32.600
And, the industrial hygiene laboratory proves
the existence of health hazards

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:34.159
which must be eliminated.

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:52.400
A still further service of the health department
is the distribution of certain drugs, vaccines,

00:17:52.490 --> 00:17:58.380
and serum to doctors for use on those who
cannot afford to pay for them. Thus, no one

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:01.519
need be denied the benefits of modern medicine.

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:07.460
Fortunate, indeed, are the Browns to have
this intensive health protection once available

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:11.120
only to city dwellers.

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:19.480
For the families that dwell in the great rural
areas, or along the shaded main streets of

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:24.820
our small towns, adequate full-time health
work has not existed for so very long. In

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:27.390
many areas, it does not exist yet.

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:32.590
Even though this is an age of speed, distances
in the country are too great for health activity

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:36.310
to be carried out with maximum effectiveness
from a central location

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:38.220
such as the health department.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:42.510
To accomplish the most good, health activity
must be localized. It must serve the people

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:45.490
of one county or a few counties combined to
make a district.

00:18:45.490 --> 00:18:50.559
Thus does it establish the intimacy and thoroughness
which ensure maximum effectiveness.

00:18:51.500 --> 00:19:00.180
The staff of the local health department,
its director, its public health nurses,

00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:10.700
its sanitary officers, and its clerical force
are all in health work on a full-time basis.

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:20.360
They have been carefully [inaudible] in the
best universities,

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:24.780
and through lectures, they keep up with the newest developments in their field.

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:30.760
Naturally, thus equipped and thus devoted,
they will do a good job of protecting the

00:19:30.769 --> 00:19:35.789
health of the people they serve. Does organized local health work pay?

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:38.460
[Bar graph is displayed with title "Diphtheria:  Deaths in Five Indiana Counties."]

00:19:38.580 --> 00:19:43.000
These figures show how deaths from certain diseases have been reduced as a result of

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:49.309
instituting full-time health work. Behind
these cold statistics is the story of reduction

00:19:49.309 --> 00:19:52.149
of needless suffering and preventable death.

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:25.720
[Bar graph with title "Typhoid: Deaths in
Five Indiana Counties."]

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:40.730
You there, are you protected like the Browns
by organized local health service? If so,

00:20:40.730 --> 00:20:45.370
cooperate with it in every way you can. If
not, who then is responsible for your community's

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:50.590
health? Are you getting the health protection
you ought to have?

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:58.240
[The End]

00:20:58.240 --> 00:21:00.240
 

